<title>CANADA: Corporate Foods plans C$25 mln bakery.</title>
<headline>Corporate Foods plans C$25 mln bakery.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Corporate Foods Ltd said on Thursday it planned to build a C$25 million bakery in Calgary, Alberta.</p>
<p>Corporate Foods, 69-percent owned by Maple Leaf Foods Inc, said the 100,000-square-foot facility would produce fresh and frozen bakery products for Canadian, United States and other export markets.</p>
<p>The bakery was expected to be operational in mid-1997, the company said. ((-- Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
